<section class="project-story model-workflows" id="model-collaboration" aria-labelledby="model-workflows-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">A WORKFLOW SKETCH</p>
  <h2 id="model-workflows-title">Who does what?</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>A diagram I came across splits the work among a human, Claude, Gemini, and Codex. My version is a little smaller: one Bear wearing two hats, and Codex holding the toolbox.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="model-workflow-grid">
    <section class="model-workflow-card" aria-labelledby="model-workflow-original">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / ENGLISH TRANSLATION</p>
      <h3 id="model-workflow-original">The multi-model workflow</h3>
      <ol class="workflow-flow" id="multi-model-flow" aria-label="Multi-model flow diagram, read from top to bottom">
        <li>{{ flowStage("01 · Frame the task") }}{{ flowNode("Human → Claude", "Request → clarify and inspect", "lead") }}</li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("02 · Compare alternatives") }}
          <div class="flow-fork" aria-label="Two independent proposals">
            {{ flowNode("Claude", "Plan A", "lead") }}
            {{ flowNode("Gemini 4 Neon", "Plan B", "second") }}
          </div>
          <div class="flow-next">
            {{ flowNode("Claude → Human", "Reconcile plans → approve direction", "human") }}
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("03 · Critique the design") }}
          {{ flowNode("Claude → Gemini → Claude", "Draft → critique → revise", "second") }}
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("04 · Build and test") }}
          {{ flowNode("Claude", "Define interfaces and acceptance checks", "lead") }}
          <div class="flow-next"><div class="flow-fork" aria-label="Frontend and backend tracks">
            {{ flowNode("Claude", "Build frontend", "lead") }}
            {{ flowNode("Codex · Astra", "Build backend", "build") }}
          </div></div>
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Claude", "Review changes and run independent tests", "lead") }}</div>
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("05 · Ship and verify") }}
          {{ flowNode("Codex · Sol", "Review PR (up to two rounds)", "build") }}
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Release pipeline", "Checks → merge → publish → verify live", "release") }}</div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <details class="flow-details">
        <summary>Read the full workflow</summary>
        <ol class="flow-transcript">
        <li><strong>State the request.</strong> I describe what I need. Claude leads: it clarifies the request, inspects the code and data, and checks what’s live.</li>
        <li><strong>Write two plans.</strong> Claude and Gemini 4 Neon each propose a plan independently. Claude compares them point by point, combines them, and records whose ideas made it in and why the others didn’t. I make the call.</li>
        <li><strong>Draft and critique.</strong> Claude drafts the design. Gemini reviews the interactions and copy. Claude decides what to keep and revises the design.</li>
        <li><strong>Define and build.</strong> Claude sets the interfaces and acceptance criteria, then hands well-defined backend pieces to Codex (GPT‑6.2 Astra). Codex reports back. Claude reads the changes, runs its own tests, and writes the frontend itself.</li>
        <li><strong>Ship and verify.</strong> Once a pull request is opened, the diagram shows an automated sequence: Codex review (GPT‑6.2 Sol, up to two rounds), automated checks, merge, publish, and verify on the live site.</li>
      </ol>
      </details>
      <p class="model-workflow-note">Translated from the supplied Chinese diagram. Model labels are kept as shown in the source.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="model-workflow-card model-workflow-bear" aria-labelledby="model-workflow-bear">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / MY VERSION</p>
      <h3 id="model-workflow-bear">Bear + Codex</h3>
      <ol class="workflow-flow" id="bear-codex-flow" aria-label="Bear and Codex flow diagram, read from top to bottom">
        <li>{{ flowStage("01 · Frame the task") }}{{ flowNode("Bear → Codex", "Question and constraints → inspect existing work", "human") }}</li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("02 · Compare alternatives") }}
          <div class="flow-fork" aria-label="Two hats worn by the same person">
            {{ flowNode("Bear · Lead hat", "Propose a plan", "lead") }}
            {{ flowNode("Bear · Critic hat", "Challenge it", "second") }}
          </div>
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Bear + Codex", "Check feasibility; Bear picks a direction", "human") }}</div>
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("03 · Critique the draft") }}
          {{ flowNode("Codex → Bear", "Show a draft, plot, or prototype → review", "build") }}
          <p class="flow-repeat"><span aria-hidden="true">↺</span> Revise and review again if needed</p>
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("04 · Build and test") }}
          {{ flowNode("Bear", "Set the acceptance criteria", "human") }}
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Codex", "Implement, test, and show the evidence", "build") }}</div>
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Bear", "Review the result in context", "human") }}</div>
        </li>
        <li>{{ flowStage("05 · Ship and verify") }}
          {{ flowNode("Bear", "Decide whether it is ready to share", "human") }}
          <div class="flow-next">{{ flowNode("Codex", "PR → checks → publish when approved → verify live", "release") }}</div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <details class="flow-details">
        <summary>Read the full workflow</summary>
        <ol class="flow-transcript">
        <li><strong>State the request.</strong> I bring the question, the constraints, and what I’d count as a useful result. Codex checks the existing work and flags what’s missing.</li>
        <li><strong>Put alternatives side by side.</strong> I play both Claude and Gemini here, somewhat less brilliantly. I frame the plan, argue against it, and decide what to try. Codex helps check what’s feasible.</li>
        <li><strong>Review something real.</strong> Codex brings back a draft, plot, or prototype. I look for what doesn’t make sense and decide what needs another pass.</li>
        <li><strong>Define and build.</strong> I spell out what must be true before I call it done. Codex implements the pieces, runs the checks, and shows me the evidence. I review the result in context.</li>
        <li><strong>Ship and verify.</strong> For changes I’m ready to publish, Codex can open the pull request, run the checks, and verify what’s actually live. I decide when the result is ready to share.</li>
      </ol>
      </details>
      <p class="model-workflow-note">One Bear, two hats. Having to explain why I picked one plan over another is the part worth keeping.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
